ow trust and you know a group dynamic  so you know that was a big challenge I  had about a day and a half with Sydney  and Talia to rehearse and what I did was  I wanted them to have a secret history  you know that only they knew  and a bomb that were you know existed  between them I'm set and nobody else on  the crew so I gave them each a notebook  and I wrote down some writing prompts  that were very personal and I left them  alone and let them write and share and  they you know through that exercise I  think got to know each other and you  know realized they had so much in common  and were able to form you know a  connection just because you are both  fairly new to the scene I want to ask  you this and you know make each other  blush can you each tell me something  about the other just I don't know a  hobby and interest you know something  that makes you super passionate about  filmmaking the movie that got you into  it anything at all I don't know Sydney's  a really really talented musician and  the first time that we hung out and we  did that writing prompt she she showed  me her album it was on Apple music and I  remember like the train ride home I like  I was listening because I listen to  music on the train I put it in and I was  like holy [ __ ] with this girl and she's  just so talented I remember being really  impressed with Thalia and how much she  had done like for her age and I thought  that was like super cool and she's also  just like a really light hearted person  and so easy to be around  and she also has a great sense of style  I love that so now we know a little bit  about you guys I am curious though I  asked us a lot because I love learning  about other members of the crew who  really contributed and there was one  person in particular I'm curious if you  bring up that I was reading about in the  press notes but if you had a name and  unsung hero of the production someone  who was really instrumental to bringing  this film to screen so successfully who  would you each pick and why tricky  because it really took an army to put  the movie together so it's hard to  really single one person I will say that  I'm Matt Rose Garnett who works for the  BBC at a coffee shop or like a  restaurant in London when I was  premiering be chats and it was one of  the most lovely kind of short meetings  and she said what do you want to do next  I said this is what I want to do and she  got behind it immediately and it was a  very transparent and supportive and  trusting collaboration and I've just  never had something so flawless and  effortless I guess and she's a magnetic  human being and really helped motivate  and inspire other people to take the  project seriously I'd say for me it was  probably a couple of the PAS  because they were there with me a lot of  the time the drives to set and home and  going around and they were like the  people I could talk to you and then  we're always like supportive and there  for me you know and like all the  in-between moments however I would say  the same - I mean yes please yes please  okay definitely one of them would be  Nikki I'm not sure if I remember all  their last names right now Nikki Bruno  and then also I've showed Alejandro the  assistant director because he was so  amazing but there's just so many people  I can name and it's just like all of  them  created such a great environment to be  in to do something so new and stressful  you know yeah same also Helen who worked  in crafty I don't know they just made  being on set so much fun what was the  key to Helen making an impression I cry  because I really do genuinely feel like  craft services very undervalued and  that's such an important thing about  keeping you going throughout the day so  how did Helen make your day I know she  always got us like dope snacks we were  just like hang out and just chill all  the time I was really fun yeah she was a  awesome person yeah I wrote her a poem  as a wrap gift and she was definit